# TCC Billing – Android app (WebView)

This is a thin app that opens your deployed site (set in `MainActivity.java`, `START_URL`).
Because it just shows the live site, every website update shows up in the app automatically.
You only rebuild the app if you change this Android code or the site address.

## Build the APK
1. Install Android Studio (it includes everything else, including the JDK).
2. File > Open > choose this `android-app` folder. Let Gradle sync finish
   (accept any "install missing SDK 34" or "upgrade plugin" prompts).
3. Build > Build Bundle(s) / APK(s) > Build APK(s).
4. When it finishes, click "locate". The file is `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`.
5. Copy it to the phone and tap it to install (allow "install unknown apps" when asked).

Needs Android 10 or newer.

## What works inside the app
- Sign in stays remembered, same as the website.
- Receipt PDFs and CSV exports are saved to **Downloads/TCC Billing** on the phone.
- The back button goes back, then asks to press again to exit.
- If there is no internet, a "Try again" screen shows.
- The Print buttons are turned off inside the app (Android WebView cannot print). Use Download PDF.